WEBVTT

00:00:20.061 --> 00:00:21.469
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:24.531 --> 00:00:26.511
Take your brother outside
as fast as you  can!

00:00:26.653 --> 00:00:27.633
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:29.546 --> 00:00:30.750
Mary! No!

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:33.873
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:35.241 --> 00:00:36.486
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:38.582 --> 00:00:40.010
I swore I was done hunting.

00:00:40.725 --> 00:00:41.806
I can't do this alone.

00:00:44.413 --> 00:00:45.086
No!

00:00:47.903 --> 00:00:49.025
We got work to do.

00:00:49.692 --> 00:00:52.121
This is dad's single
most valuable possession

00:00:52.162 --> 00:00:54.325
Everything he knows about
every evil thing is in here.

00:00:54.488 --> 00:00:56.407
I think he wants us to
pick up where he left off

00:00:56.529 --> 00:00:58.856
You know, saving people, hunting things,

00:00:58.931 --> 00:00:59.870
Family business.

00:00:59.911 --> 00:01:01.768
No. I got to find Jessica's killer.

00:01:01.788 --> 00:01:03.319
It's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.136
Sam, You know we're
gonna find dad, right?

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:07.946
Yeah. I know.

00:01:17.485 --> 00:01:19.403
Okay, your turn. Truth or dare?

00:01:19.826 --> 00:01:20.479
Truth.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:23.152
Do you want to make
out with benji swartz?

00:01:24.479 --> 00:01:25.091
Dare.

00:01:25.642 --> 00:01:26.806
Okay, lame.

00:01:27.718 --> 00:01:28.901
You have to...

00:01:29.983 --> 00:01:31.759
Say "bloody mary" in the bathroom.

00:01:32.426 --> 00:01:34.345
Is that the best you can come up with?

00:01:34.712 --> 00:01:35.855
Who's bloody mary?

00:01:36.365 --> 00:01:37.692
She's this witch.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.958
I heard she was a lady
killed in a car crash.

00:01:40.447 --> 00:01:41.815
It doesn't matter who she is.

00:01:42.267 --> 00:01:44.961
If you say her name three
times in the bathroom mirror,

00:01:45.777 --> 00:01:46.899
She appears...

00:01:47.593 --> 00:01:48.900
And scratches your eyes out!

00:01:51.656 --> 00:01:53.432
So why would anyone say it?

00:01:54.126 --> 00:01:55.616
Because it isn't real.

00:01:57.044 --> 00:01:58.371
No turning on the lights.

00:01:58.990 --> 00:01:59.949
And remember,

00:02:00.112 --> 00:02:00.949
Three times.

00:02:26.765 --> 00:02:27.704
Bloody mary.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:30.785
This is so stupid.

00:02:34.791 --> 00:02:35.729
Bloody mary.

00:02:46.423 --> 00:02:47.444
Bloody mary.

00:02:58.146 --> 00:02:58.799
Scared you.

00:02:58.922 --> 00:03:00.105
You guys are jerks.

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.065
Lily?

00:03:01.738 --> 00:03:02.779
You mind keeping it down?

00:03:03.657 --> 00:03:04.657
Sorry, daddy.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.494
Sorry, mr. Shoemaker.

00:03:44.803 --> 00:03:46.191
You so like him!

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.899
Hey, geek.

00:03:49.144 --> 00:03:50.491
You guys having fun?

00:03:50.818 --> 00:03:52.103
You're out past curfew.

00:03:52.812 --> 00:03:53.669
Thanks, dad.

00:04:35.611 --> 00:04:36.754
Why Sam?

00:04:38.741 --> 00:04:39.353
No!

00:04:42.735 --> 00:04:44.551
Why Sam? Sam, wake up.

00:04:53.363 --> 00:04:55.261
I take it I was having a nightmare?

00:04:56.098 --> 00:04:57.649
Yeah, another one.

00:05:01.276 --> 00:05:02.746
Hey, at least I got some sleep.

00:05:02.909 --> 00:05:05.175
Hey, you know, sooner or later,
we're gonna talk about this.

00:05:06.134 --> 00:05:06.848
Are we here?

00:05:07.256 --> 00:05:09.726
Yep. Welcome to Toledo, Ohio.

00:05:13.421 --> 00:05:15.523
So, what do you think
really happened to this guy?

00:05:15.557 --> 00:05:17.170
So what we're gonna find out.

00:05:19.721 --> 00:05:20.517
Let's go.

00:05:49.742 --> 00:05:50.253
Hey.

00:05:50.987 --> 00:05:51.600
Hey.

00:05:53.008 --> 00:05:53.763
Can I help you?

00:05:54.416 --> 00:05:56.478
Yeah, we're the... med students.

00:05:56.985 --> 00:05:57.557
Sorry?

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:58.822
Oh, doctor...

00:05:59.455 --> 00:06:01.067
Fliglavitch didn't tell you?

00:06:01.128 --> 00:06:03.026
We talked to him on the phone.

00:06:03.169 --> 00:06:04.394
We're from Ohio state.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:06.737
He's supposed to show
us the shoemaker corpse.

00:06:06.758 --> 00:06:07.513
It's for our paper.

00:06:07.778 --> 00:06:09.574
Well, I'm sorry, he's at lunch.

00:06:09.738 --> 00:06:10.391
Oh.

00:06:10.534 --> 00:06:11.615
Well, he said, uh

00:06:11.840 --> 00:06:13.064
Oh, well, you know, it doesn't matter.

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.533
You don't mind showing
us the body, do you?

00:06:15.574 --> 00:06:16.798
Sorry, I can't.

00:06:17.002 --> 00:06:19.268
Doc will be back in an
hour. You can wait for him,

00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:20.023
If you want.

00:06:20.186 --> 00:06:20.941
An hour?

00:06:22.312 --> 00:06:24.046
We got to be heading back to columbus.

00:06:24.108 --> 00:06:24.740
Yeah.

00:06:25.434 --> 00:06:27.087
Look man, this paper's half our grade,

00:06:27.128 --> 00:06:28.904
So if you don't mind
helping us out? Look, man

00:06:30.159 --> 00:06:30.914
No.

00:06:33.302 --> 00:06:35.160
I'm gonna hit him in his face, I swear.

00:06:49.052 --> 00:06:50.093
Follow me.

00:06:53.985 --> 00:06:55.522
Dude, I earned that money.

00:06:55.639 --> 00:06:57.169
You won it in a poker game.

00:06:57.394 --> 00:06:58.190
Yeah.

00:06:58.904 --> 00:07:00.802
The newspaper said
his daughter found him.

00:07:01.204 --> 00:07:02.755
She said his eyes were bleeding.

00:07:02.837 --> 00:07:03.898
More than that.

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.572
They practically liquefied.

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:12.385
Any sign of a struggle,
maybe somebody did it to him?

00:07:12.566 --> 00:07:13.239
Nope.

00:07:13.648 --> 00:07:15.342
Besides the daughter, he was all alone.

00:07:16.168 --> 00:07:17.805
What's the official causeof death?

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.963
Doc's not sure. He's
thinking massive stroke,

00:07:20.987 --> 00:07:22.554
Maybe an aneurysm.

00:07:23.232 --> 00:07:24.870
Something burst up in
there, that's for sure.

00:07:25.448 --> 00:07:26.337
What do you mean?

00:07:26.828 --> 00:07:28.606
Intense cerebral bleeding.

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:31.389
This guy had more blooding his
skull than anyone I've ever seen.

00:07:32.325 --> 00:07:33.284
But the eyes?

00:07:33.635 --> 00:07:35.085
What would cause something like that?

00:07:35.283 --> 00:07:36.850
Capillaries can burst.

00:07:36.897 --> 00:07:38.862
See a lot of bloodshot
eyes with stroke victims.

00:07:39.213 --> 00:07:41.341
Yeah, you ever see exploding eyeballs?

00:07:41.879 --> 00:07:43.260
That's a first for me.

00:07:43.377 --> 00:07:45.037
But, hey, I'm not the doctor.

00:07:46.538 --> 00:07:48.644
Think we could take a
look atthat police report?

00:07:48.761 --> 00:07:50.398
You know, for our paper?

00:07:51.264 --> 00:07:53.603
I'm not really supposed to show you

00:07:57.702 --> 00:07:59.199
Might not be one of ours.

00:07:59.293 --> 00:08:01.257
Might just be some freak medical thing.

00:08:01.749 --> 00:08:03.198
How many times in dad's long

00:08:03.199 --> 00:08:06.333
And varied career has it actually
been a freak medical thing

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:09.554
And not some sign of an
awful supernatural death?

00:08:09.694 --> 00:08:11.636
Uh, almost never.

00:08:11.823 --> 00:08:12.829
Exactly.

00:08:12.946 --> 00:08:13.811
All right.

00:08:14.115 --> 00:08:15.628
Let's go talk to the daughter.

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.414
Feel like we're underdressed.

00:08:44.761 --> 00:08:46.087
You must be Donna,right?

00:08:46.274 --> 00:08:46.883
Yeah.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:50.859
Hi, uh... We're really sorry.

00:08:51.748 --> 00:08:52.520
Thank you.

00:08:53.035 --> 00:08:54.976
I'm sam.This is dean.

00:08:55.871 --> 00:08:57.134
We worked with your dad.

00:08:58.467 --> 00:08:59.262
You did?

00:08:59.590 --> 00:09:00.830
Yeah.This whole thing

00:09:01.625 --> 00:09:02.795
I mean, a stroke.

00:09:04.381 --> 00:09:06.322
I don't think she really wants
to talk about this right now.

00:09:06.323 --> 00:09:07.609
It's okay, I'm okay.

00:09:09.294 --> 00:09:10.674
Were there ever any symptoms?

00:09:10.791 --> 00:09:12.078
Dizziness, migraines?

00:09:13.154 --> 00:09:14.019
No.

00:09:15.233 --> 00:09:17.175
That's because it wasn't a stroke.

00:09:17.409 --> 00:09:18.415
Lily, don't say that.

00:09:18.672 --> 00:09:19.374
What?

00:09:20.169 --> 00:09:21.666
I'm sorry, she's just upset.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.654
No, it happened because of me.

00:09:23.725 --> 00:09:24.988
Sweetie, it didn't.

00:09:25.069 --> 00:09:25.865
Lily,

00:09:26.866 --> 00:09:28.621
Why would you saysomething like that?

00:09:29.559 --> 00:09:31.173
Right before he died,I said it.

00:09:31.875 --> 00:09:32.694
You said what?

00:09:33.419 --> 00:09:35.922
Bloody Mary, three times
in the bathroom mirror.

00:09:39.353 --> 00:09:41.014
She took his eyes, that's what she does.

00:09:41.084 --> 00:09:43.494
That's not why dad
died.This isn't your fault.

00:09:44.219 --> 00:09:45.739
I think your sister's right,lily.

00:09:46.621 --> 00:09:48.749
There's no way it could
have been Bloody Mary.

00:09:49.896 --> 00:09:52.118
Your dad didn't say it,did he?

00:09:53.849 --> 00:09:55.322
No, I don't think so.

00:10:20.615 --> 00:10:21.972
Sam:The Bloody Mary legend

00:10:23.808 --> 00:10:26.299
Dad ever find any evidence
that it was a real thing?

00:10:27.094 --> 00:10:28.357
Not that I know of.

00:10:33.602 --> 00:10:34.397
I mean,

00:10:34.912 --> 00:10:35.988
Everywhere else,

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:41.126
All over the country,
kids will play Bloody Mary.

00:10:41.127 --> 00:10:43.373
And as far as we know,
nobody dies from it.

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:45.209
Hey well, maybe everywhere
it's just a story,

00:10:45.232 --> 00:10:46.846
But here it's actually happening.

00:10:46.940 --> 00:10:48.530
The place where the legend began?

00:10:49.856 --> 00:10:52.079
But according to the legend,
the person who says...

00:10:55.166 --> 00:10:57.880
The person who says
you know what gets it

00:10:57.903 --> 00:10:58.488
But here...

00:10:58.511 --> 00:11:00.055
Shoemaker gets it instead,yeah.

00:11:00.102 --> 00:11:00.710
Right.

00:11:01.739 --> 00:11:03.540
Never heard anything like that before.

00:11:04.352 --> 00:11:06.832
Still, the guy did die
right in front of the mirror.

00:11:07.031 --> 00:11:09.229
And the daughter's right.
The way the legend goes,

00:11:09.924 --> 00:11:11.772
"You know who" scratches your eyes out.

00:11:11.936 --> 00:11:13.292
It's worth checking into.

00:11:20.380 --> 00:11:21.479
What are you doingup here?

00:11:22.819 --> 00:11:23.590
We...

00:11:24.175 --> 00:11:25.555
We had to go to the bathroom.

00:11:26.585 --> 00:11:27.520
Who are you?

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:31.076
Like we said downstairs,
we worked with Donna's dad.

00:11:31.380 --> 00:11:33.953
He was a day trader or
something, he worked by himself.

00:11:34.236 --> 00:11:35.733
No, I know, I meant...

00:11:35.896 --> 00:11:37.955
And those weird questions downstairs,

00:11:38.914 --> 00:11:39.990
What was that?

00:11:42.072 --> 00:11:43.896
So you tell me what's going on

00:11:44.508 --> 00:11:45.654
Or I start screaming.

00:11:45.888 --> 00:11:47.011
All right, all right.

00:11:49.329 --> 00:11:51.411
We think something
happened to Donna's dad.

00:11:51.528 --> 00:11:52.604
Yeah, a stroke.

00:11:52.931 --> 00:11:54.756
That's not the sign of a typical stroke.

00:11:57.142 --> 00:11:58.639
We think it might be something else.

00:11:59.364 --> 00:12:00.129
Like what?

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:01.743
Honestly,

00:12:02.936 --> 00:12:03.965
We don't know yet.

00:12:05.088 --> 00:12:07.193
But we don't want it to
happen to anyone else.

00:12:07.661 --> 00:12:08.496
That's the truth.

00:12:09.408 --> 00:12:10.063
So,

00:12:10.601 --> 00:12:11.794
If you're gonna scream,

00:12:12.590 --> 00:12:13.736
Go right ahead.

00:12:16.332 --> 00:12:17.331
Who are you, cops?

00:12:19.857 --> 00:12:20.746
Something like that.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:21.869
I'll tell you what.

00:12:22.126 --> 00:12:22.781
Here.

00:12:23.249 --> 00:12:24.477
If you think of anything,

00:12:24.547 --> 00:12:26.489
You or your friends
notice anything strange,

00:12:26.769 --> 00:12:29.062
Out of the ordinary,
just give us a call.

00:12:37.529 --> 00:12:39.627
All right, say Bloody Mary
really is haunting this town.

00:12:39.651 --> 00:12:41.639
There's gonna be some sort of proof

00:12:41.733 --> 00:12:43.136
A local woman who died nasty.

00:12:43.276 --> 00:12:45.171
Yeah, but a legend this
wide spread, it's hard.

00:12:45.194 --> 00:12:47.532
I mean, there's like 50
versions of who she actually is.

00:12:47.533 --> 00:12:48.690
One story says she's a witch,

00:12:48.691 --> 00:12:50.866
Another says she's a mutilated bride.

00:12:50.960 --> 00:12:51.989
There's a lot more.

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:53.720
What are we supposed to be looking for?

00:12:53.854 --> 00:12:55.679
Every version's got thingsin common.

00:12:55.702 --> 00:12:56.918
It's always a woman named Mary,

00:12:56.930 --> 00:12:59.035
And she always dies
in front of a mirror.

00:12:59.550 --> 00:13:01.251
So we've got to search local newspapers

00:13:01.274 --> 00:13:03.192
Public records as far back as they go,

00:13:03.286 --> 00:13:05.157
See if we can find a
Mary who fits the bill.

00:13:05.789 --> 00:13:06.888
Well, that sounds annoying.

00:13:07.075 --> 00:13:08.689
No, it won't be so bad,

00:13:08.759 --> 00:13:09.718
As long as we...

00:13:11.690 --> 00:13:12.556
I take it back.

00:13:13.234 --> 00:13:14.661
This will be very annoying.

00:13:17.702 --> 00:13:20.848
I'm not sure. They were cops
or detectives or something.

00:13:21.129 --> 00:13:23.047
Whoever they were, they were cute.

00:13:23.164 --> 00:13:23.912
Jill.

00:13:24.029 --> 00:13:24.989
You didn't think so?

00:13:25.224 --> 00:13:27.025
Yeah, okay,they were cute. But,

00:13:27.836 --> 00:13:30.760
Still,do you think something
could have happenedto Donna's dad?

00:13:30.894 --> 00:13:32.280
Maybe Lily was right.

00:13:32.882 --> 00:13:34.730
Maybe Bloody Mary got him.

00:13:35.666 --> 00:13:36.665
Very funny.

00:13:37.811 --> 00:13:39.729
Wait, I'm sorry.

00:13:40.454 --> 00:13:42.653
Was that fear I hear in your voice?

00:13:43.261 --> 00:13:44.033
No.

00:13:45.359 --> 00:13:46.178
Charlie...

00:13:46.412 --> 00:13:48.260
I'm walking to the
bathroom mirror right now.

00:13:49.149 --> 00:13:50.295
Jill, quit it.

00:13:53.003 --> 00:13:54.032
Oh, no,

00:13:54.383 --> 00:13:55.670
I can't help myself.

00:13:56.535 --> 00:13:57.822
I'm gonna say it.

00:13:58.898 --> 00:13:59.857
Bloody Mary.

00:14:00.692 --> 00:14:02.072
Bloody Mary.

00:14:03.055 --> 00:14:04.973
Bloody Mary.

00:14:07.352 --> 00:14:08.171
Jill?

00:14:13.107 --> 00:14:13.878
Jill!

00:14:18.422 --> 00:14:20.574
You're such a freak.
I'll call you tomorrow.

00:15:16.175 --> 00:15:17.321
You did it.

00:15:22.257 --> 00:15:23.695
You killed that boy.

00:15:43.741 --> 00:15:44.654
Why Sam?

00:15:49.581 --> 00:15:50.985
Why'd you let me fall asleep?

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.207
'Cause I'm an awesome brother.

00:15:55.317 --> 00:15:56.790
So, what did you dream about?

00:15:57.562 --> 00:15:59.387
Lollipops and candy canes.

00:16:01.094 --> 00:16:02.170
Yeah, sure.

00:16:06.605 --> 00:16:07.774
You find anything?

00:16:08.078 --> 00:16:10.464
Oh, besides a whole new
level of frustration?

00:16:10.979 --> 00:16:13.061
No. I've looked at everything.

00:16:15.158 --> 00:16:17.615
A few local women, a
Laura and a Catherine,

00:16:17.638 --> 00:16:19.463
Committed suicide in front of a mirror,

00:16:19.884 --> 00:16:21.935
And a giant mirror fell
on a guy named dave.

00:16:22.029 --> 00:16:22.918
But, uh...

00:16:24.064 --> 00:16:24.836
No Mary.

00:16:29.163 --> 00:16:30.824
Maybe we just haven't found it yet.

00:16:32.087 --> 00:16:34.192
I've also been searching
for strange deaths,

00:16:34.276 --> 00:16:35.843
In the area, you know,

00:16:36.197 --> 00:16:37.858
Eyeball bleeding, that sort of thing.

00:16:37.998 --> 00:16:39.027
There's nothing.

00:16:39.869 --> 00:16:41.834
Whatever's happening here,
maybe it just ain't Mary.

00:16:48.337 --> 00:16:49.039
Hello?

00:16:56.511 --> 00:16:59.295
And they found her
on the bathroom floor.

00:17:00.441 --> 00:17:03.435
And her-Her eyes...

00:17:04.956 --> 00:17:06.430
They were gone.

00:17:07.295 --> 00:17:08.161
I'm sorry.

00:17:10.453 --> 00:17:11.576
And she said it.

00:17:13.447 --> 00:17:14.937
I heard her say it.

00:17:16.500 --> 00:17:18.152
But it couldn't be because of that.

00:17:21.534 --> 00:17:22.633
I'm insane, right?

00:17:24.545 --> 00:17:25.644
No, you're not insane.

00:17:26.673 --> 00:17:29.457
God, that makes me feel so much worse.

00:17:30.432 --> 00:17:31.227
Look...

00:17:34.549 --> 00:17:36.245
We think something's happening here,

00:17:37.485 --> 00:17:39.075
Something that can't be explained.

00:17:40.191 --> 00:17:41.244
And we're gonna stop it,

00:17:42.437 --> 00:17:43.513
But we could use your help.

00:18:02.081 --> 00:18:03.578
What did you tell Jill's mom?

00:18:03.625 --> 00:18:06.245
I just said I needed some time alone
with Jill's pictures and things.

00:18:06.278 --> 00:18:06.980
Great.

00:18:07.471 --> 00:18:08.734
I hate lying to her.

00:18:09.389 --> 00:18:10.746
This is for the greater good.

00:18:10.793 --> 00:18:11.775
Hit the lights.

00:18:16.072 --> 00:18:17.499
What are you guys looking for?

00:18:17.990 --> 00:18:19.784
We'll let you know
as soon as we find it.

00:18:19.854 --> 00:18:21.164
Hey, night vision.

00:18:23.036 --> 00:18:24.696
Thanks. Perfect.

00:18:27.974 --> 00:18:29.284
Do I look like Paris Hilton?

00:18:40.969 --> 00:18:42.700
So, I don't get it.

00:18:42.724 --> 00:18:45.133
I mean, the first victim
didn't summon Mary,

00:18:45.157 --> 00:18:46.794
And the second victim did.

00:18:47.145 --> 00:18:48.431
How's she choosing them?

00:18:48.969 --> 00:18:49.695
Beats me.

00:18:54.257 --> 00:18:56.245
I want to know why Jill
said it in the first place.

00:18:57.415 --> 00:18:58.444
It's just a joke.

00:18:58.811 --> 00:19:01.688
Somebody's gonna say it again.
It's just a matter of time.

00:19:14.372 --> 00:19:15.051
Hey.

00:19:16.470 --> 00:19:17.897
There's a black light
in the trunk, right?

00:19:40.591 --> 00:19:42.299
Gary Bryman?

00:19:43.936 --> 00:19:45.163
You know who that is?

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:47.222
No.

00:19:55.021 --> 00:19:58.202
So, Gary Bryman was an 8 year-Old boy.

00:19:59.115 --> 00:20:01.197
Two years ago, he was
killed in a hit and run.

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:04.121
The car was described
as a black toyota camry,

00:20:04.722 --> 00:20:07.178
But nobody got the
plates or saw the driver.

00:20:07.506 --> 00:20:08.348
Oh, my god.

00:20:09.307 --> 00:20:09.915
What?

00:20:10.359 --> 00:20:11.763
Jill drove that car.

00:20:14.975 --> 00:20:16.729
We need to get back to
your friend Donna's house.

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:27.311
Linda shoemaker.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.177
Why are you asking me this?

00:20:32.539 --> 00:20:34.567
Look, we're sorry, but it's important.

00:20:35.666 --> 00:20:36.321
Yeah.

00:20:36.622 --> 00:20:37.956
Linda's my mom, okay?

00:20:38.283 --> 00:20:40.178
And she overdosed on sleeping pills.

00:20:40.295 --> 00:20:41.979
It was an accident, and that's it.

00:20:45.311 --> 00:20:46.270
I think you should leave.

00:20:46.293 --> 00:20:48.071
Donna, just listen Get out of my house!

00:20:52.392 --> 00:20:53.304
Oh, my god.

00:20:54.591 --> 00:20:57.222
Do you really think her dad
could have killed her mom?

00:20:58.603 --> 00:20:59.538
Maybe.

00:21:00.151 --> 00:21:01.531
I think I should stick around.

00:21:03.168 --> 00:21:04.805
All right. Whatever you do, don't...

00:21:04.993 --> 00:21:07.308
Believe me, I won't say it.

00:21:11.618 --> 00:21:12.811
Wait, wait, wait.

00:21:13.116 --> 00:21:15.057
You're doing a nationwide search?

00:21:15.197 --> 00:21:15.829
Yep.

00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:18.675
The NCIC, the FBI database

00:21:18.868 --> 00:21:22.084
Any mary in the country who died in
front of a mirror is good enough for me.

00:21:22.494 --> 00:21:25.464
But if she's haunting the town,
she should have died in the town.

00:21:25.623 --> 00:21:28.547
I'm telling you. There's nothing local. I
check. So, unless you've gota better idea.

00:21:28.659 --> 00:21:31.003
Why Mary's choosing a victim?
It seems like there's a pattern.

00:21:31.043 --> 00:21:32.245
I know I was thinking the same thing.

00:21:32.325 --> 00:21:34.329
With mr. Shoemaker
and Jill's hit and run

00:21:34.349 --> 00:21:35.871
Both had secrets where people died.

00:21:35.931 --> 00:21:36.432
Right.

00:21:36.512 --> 00:21:37.896
There's a lot of folklore about mirrors

00:21:37.897 --> 00:21:39.900
That they reveal or your
lies, or your secrets,

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:42.023
That they're a true
reflection of your soul,

00:21:42.024 --> 00:21:43.466
Which is why it's bad
luck to break them.

00:21:43.546 --> 00:21:44.408
Right. Right.

00:21:45.282 --> 00:21:46.644
Yeah, so maybe if you've got a secret,

00:21:46.664 --> 00:21:48.498
I mean, like a really nasty
one where someone died,

00:21:48.499 --> 00:21:50.903
Then mary sees it and
punishes you for it.

00:21:51.035 --> 00:21:52.736
Whether you summoned her or not.

00:21:53.619 --> 00:21:54.601
Take a look at this.

00:22:07.305 --> 00:22:08.908
Looks like the same handprint.

00:22:09.370 --> 00:22:11.073
Her name was Mary Worthington

00:22:11.896 --> 00:22:14.120
An unsolved murder in
Fort Wayne, Indiana.

00:22:16.346 --> 00:22:19.131
I was on the job for 35 years,

00:22:19.371 --> 00:22:20.653
Detective for most of that.

00:22:21.414 --> 00:22:23.778
Now, everybody packs it
in with a few loose ends,

00:22:23.861 --> 00:22:25.784
But the Mary Worthington murder...

00:22:27.647 --> 00:22:29.030
That one still gets me.

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:30.432
What exactly happened?

00:22:31.896 --> 00:22:33.619
You boys said you were reporters.

00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:35.542
We know Mary was 19,

00:22:35.685 --> 00:22:36.787
Lived by herself.

00:22:36.927 --> 00:22:38.730
We know she won a few beauty contests,

00:22:38.790 --> 00:22:40.252
Dreamt of getting out of Indiana,

00:22:40.773 --> 00:22:41.715
Being an actress.

00:22:42.214 --> 00:22:44.258
And we know, the night of march 29th,

00:22:44.779 --> 00:22:46.161
Someone broke into her apartment

00:22:46.301 --> 00:22:47.143
And murdered her,

00:22:48.064 --> 00:22:49.266
Cut out her eyeswith a knife.

00:22:51.111 --> 00:22:51.872
That's right.

00:22:53.996 --> 00:22:56.240
See, sir, when we ask you what
happened, we want to know what

00:22:56.620 --> 00:22:57.401
You think happened.

00:23:00.971 --> 00:23:03.956
Technically, I'm not supposed
to have a copy of this.

00:23:10.106 --> 00:23:10.707
Now,

00:23:12.310 --> 00:23:13.371
See that there,

00:23:13.952 --> 00:23:14.794

"T-R-E"?

00:23:15.295 --> 00:23:15.916
Yeah.

00:23:16.647 --> 00:23:19.333
I think Mary was trying to
spell out the name of her killer.

00:23:19.414 --> 00:23:20.395
You know who it was?

00:23:20.816 --> 00:23:21.838
Not for sure.

00:23:23.340 --> 00:23:24.722
But there was a local man,

00:23:24.803 --> 00:23:25.684
A surgeon,

00:23:26.247 --> 00:23:27.269
Trevor Sampson.

00:23:27.990 --> 00:23:29.833
And I think he cut her up good.

00:23:30.314 --> 00:23:32.372
Now, why would he do
something like that?

00:23:32.913 --> 00:23:35.096
Her diary mentioned
a man she was seeing.

00:23:35.860 --> 00:23:37.723
She called him by his initial, "T."

00:23:38.524 --> 00:23:39.226
Well,

00:23:39.887 --> 00:23:41.590
Her last entry,

00:23:41.970 --> 00:23:44.915
She was gonna tell to his
wife about their affair.

00:23:45.137 --> 00:23:47.240
But how do you know it
was Sampson who killed her?

00:23:47.862 --> 00:23:49.164
It's hard to say.

00:23:51.750 --> 00:23:54.735
But the way her eyes were cut
out, it was almost professional.

00:23:55.897 --> 00:23:57.321
But you could never prove it?

00:23:57.442 --> 00:23:57.962
No.

00:23:58.443 --> 00:23:59.265
No prints,

00:23:59.365 --> 00:24:00.547
No witnesses.

00:24:01.388 --> 00:24:02.570
He was meticulous.

00:24:04.333 --> 00:24:05.395
Is he still alive?

00:24:07.236 --> 00:24:07.817
Nope.

00:24:10.642 --> 00:24:11.743
If you ask me,

00:24:12.124 --> 00:24:15.109
Mary spent her last living moments

00:24:15.572 --> 00:24:17.876
Trying to expose this guy's secret.

00:24:20.020 --> 00:24:21.222
But she never could.

00:24:23.385 --> 00:24:24.347
Where's she buried?

00:24:25.893 --> 00:24:26.695
She wasn't.

00:24:27.135 --> 00:24:27.937
She was cremated.

00:24:31.342 --> 00:24:34.027
What about that mirror?  It's not
in evidence lockup somewhere, is it?

00:24:35.847 --> 00:24:36.588
No.

00:24:37.890 --> 00:24:40.415
It was returned to Mary's
family a long time ago.

00:24:42.037 --> 00:24:44.121
You have the names of
her family by any chance?

00:24:49.391 --> 00:24:51.356
I mean, you bring these
strangers into my house,

00:24:51.376 --> 00:24:52.919
And they ask me things like that?

00:24:52.959 --> 00:24:54.261
They were only trying to help.

00:24:54.361 --> 00:24:56.425
Please, Donna, you have to believe me.

00:24:56.625 --> 00:24:58.408
What? About bloody mary?

00:24:58.650 --> 00:25:00.774
Please, I know it sounds crazy.

00:25:01.134 --> 00:25:03.057
"Crazy" doesn't even begin to cover it.

00:25:03.278 --> 00:25:05.421
I mean, it's one thing for my
sister to believe this crap.

00:25:05.523 --> 00:25:07.367
She's 12. But you?

00:25:07.889 --> 00:25:08.851
Think about the way

00:25:09.632 --> 00:25:10.553
Your dad died,

00:25:10.994 --> 00:25:13.058
Okay, and the way Jill died.

00:25:14.382 --> 00:25:15.965
Okay, so...

00:25:17.107 --> 00:25:17.667
Bloody Mary.

00:25:17.708 --> 00:25:18.068
No!

00:25:18.108 --> 00:25:20.011
Bloody Mary. Bloody Mary.

00:25:22.978 --> 00:25:24.861
See? Nothing happened.

00:25:25.322 --> 00:25:26.604
Why would you do that?

00:25:27.145 --> 00:25:28.127
Oh, my god,

00:25:28.728 --> 00:25:30.751
There really is
something wrong with you.

00:25:42.627 --> 00:25:45.572
Elements that lose electrons become

00:25:45.712 --> 00:25:47.055
Positive ions,

00:25:47.596 --> 00:25:50.701
Which are smaller than other
atoms of the same element.

00:25:51.222 --> 00:25:53.766
Therefore, the ionic radius

00:25:53.897 --> 00:25:56.201
Is smaller than the atomic radius

00:26:01.435 --> 00:26:02.276
Charlie!

00:26:07.106 --> 00:26:07.868
Charlie!

00:26:12.818 --> 00:26:15.747
Charlie, stop it! What's
wrong? Just calm down!

00:26:18.855 --> 00:26:20.134
Charlie! Aah! Let me go!

00:26:20.264 --> 00:26:21.024
Charlie!

00:26:23.323 --> 00:26:24.065
Oh, really?

00:26:24.529 --> 00:26:26.642
Ah, that's too bad, Mr. Worthington.

00:26:27.208 --> 00:26:28.951
I would have paid a lot for that mirror.

00:26:28.988 --> 00:26:30.231
Okay, well, maybe next time.

00:26:30.453 --> 00:26:31.640
All right, thanks.

00:26:31.788 --> 00:26:32.493
So?

00:26:32.697 --> 00:26:34.551
So, that was Mary's brother.

00:26:34.727 --> 00:26:37.045
The mirror was in the family for years,

00:26:37.101 --> 00:26:38.436
Until he sold it

00:26:38.695 --> 00:26:39.789
One week ago

00:26:40.883 --> 00:26:42.867
To a store called estate antiques,

00:26:43.303 --> 00:26:44.861
A store in Toledo.

00:26:46.715 --> 00:26:48.755
So wherever the mirror
goes, that's where Mary goes?

00:26:49.005 --> 00:26:51.397
Her spirit's definitely
tied up with it somehow.

00:26:51.527 --> 00:26:54.512
Isn't there an old superstition that
says mirrors can capture spirits?

00:26:55.097 --> 00:26:57.285
Yeah, there is. When
someone would die in a house,

00:26:57.322 --> 00:26:59.825
People would cover up the mirrors
so the ghost wouldn't get trapped.

00:27:00.328 --> 00:27:02.561
This Mary dies in front of the
mirror, and it draws in her spirit.

00:27:02.850 --> 00:27:05.835
Yeah, but how could she move
through 100 different mirrors?

00:27:06.484 --> 00:27:08.014
I don't know but if the
mirror is the source,

00:27:08.033 --> 00:27:09.572
I say we find it and smash it.

00:27:10.925 --> 00:27:12.464
Yeah, I don't know. Maybe.

00:27:16.678 --> 00:27:17.327
Hello?

00:27:18.773 --> 00:27:19.496
Charlie?

00:27:38.557 --> 00:27:39.298
Hey.

00:27:40.244 --> 00:27:41.264
Hey. It's okay.

00:27:42.061 --> 00:27:43.767
You can open up your eyes, Charlie.

00:27:43.814 --> 00:27:45.575
It's okay, all right?

00:27:46.929 --> 00:27:47.745
Now, listen.

00:27:48.431 --> 00:27:49.729
You're gonna stay right here

00:27:50.331 --> 00:27:51.129
On this bed.

00:27:51.731 --> 00:27:53.178
You're not gonna look at glass

00:27:53.345 --> 00:27:55.347
Or anything else that
has a reflection, okay?

00:27:56.155 --> 00:27:57.341
As long as you do that

00:27:58.157 --> 00:27:59.585
She cannot get you.

00:28:02.691 --> 00:28:04.471
But I can't keep that up forever.

00:28:07.314 --> 00:28:08.798
I'm gonna die, aren't I?

00:28:10.707 --> 00:28:11.301
No.

00:28:12.895 --> 00:28:13.581
No.

00:28:15.371 --> 00:28:16.548
Not anytime soon.

00:28:18.746 --> 00:28:19.784
All right, Charlie,

00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:21.527
We need to know what happened.

00:28:22.510 --> 00:28:23.826
We were in the bathroom.

00:28:24.077 --> 00:28:24.967
Donna said it.

00:28:25.004 --> 00:28:26.561
That's not what we're talking about.

00:28:30.029 --> 00:28:31.586
Something happened, didn't it,

00:28:33.014 --> 00:28:34.015
In your life.

00:28:35.867 --> 00:28:36.645
A secret...

00:28:37.906 --> 00:28:39.140
Where someone got hurt?

00:28:45.110 --> 00:28:46.436
Can you tell us about it?

00:28:50.553 --> 00:28:51.721
I had this boyfriend.

00:28:54.680 --> 00:28:55.570
I loved him.

00:28:57.387 --> 00:28:59.681
But he kind of scared me, too, you know?

00:29:00.690 --> 00:29:01.560
And...

00:29:01.815 --> 00:29:02.729
One night

00:29:03.281 --> 00:29:04.428
At his house,

00:29:04.746 --> 00:29:05.893
We got in this fight.

00:29:08.293 --> 00:29:09.716
Then I broke up with him,

00:29:10.905 --> 00:29:13.093
And he got upset and he said

00:29:13.369 --> 00:29:15.726
He needed me and he loved me.

00:29:17.224 --> 00:29:18.179
And he said...

00:29:19.220 --> 00:29:22.130
"Charlie, if you walk out that door
right now, I'm gonna kill myself."

00:29:24.997 --> 00:29:26.441
And you know what I said?

00:29:28.061 --> 00:29:29.335
I said, "go ahead."

00:29:32.351 --> 00:29:33.562
And I left.

00:29:36.769 --> 00:29:38.107
How could I say that?

00:29:43.406 --> 00:29:45.254
How could I leave him like that?

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:49.444
I just...

00:29:50.230 --> 00:29:52.142
I didn't believe him, you know?

00:29:59.043 --> 00:30:00.211
I should have.

00:30:09.336 --> 00:30:12.331
Her boyfriend killing himself,
that's not really Charlie's fault.

00:30:13.244 --> 00:30:14.369
You know as well as I do,

00:30:14.391 --> 00:30:17.131
Spirits don't exactly
see shades of gray,

00:30:17.194 --> 00:30:17.980
Dean.

00:30:18.373 --> 00:30:19.541
Charlie had a secret,

00:30:19.838 --> 00:30:20.815
Someone died.

00:30:21.367 --> 00:30:22.514
That's good enough for Mary.

00:30:23.321 --> 00:30:24.298
I guess.

00:30:24.957 --> 00:30:26.167
You know,I've been thinking,

00:30:27.112 --> 00:30:29.809
It might not be enough
to just smash that mirror.

00:30:30.404 --> 00:30:31.466
Why, what do you mean?

00:30:31.742 --> 00:30:33.059
Mary's hard to pin down, right?

00:30:33.123 --> 00:30:34.822
And she moves around
from mirror to mirror.

00:30:34.843 --> 00:30:37.829
So, who's to say that she's not gonna
just keep hiding in them forever?

00:30:39.252 --> 00:30:40.441
So maybe...

00:30:41.737 --> 00:30:43.245
We should try to pin her down,

00:30:44.356 --> 00:30:46.565
You know, summon her to her mirror

00:30:47.415 --> 00:30:48.604
And then smash it.

00:30:49.241 --> 00:30:50.622
Well, how do you know that's gonna work?

00:30:50.686 --> 00:30:51.471
I don't,

00:30:52.172 --> 00:30:53.383
I'm not for sure.

00:30:55.993 --> 00:30:57.352
Well, who's gonnasummon her?

00:30:59.157 --> 00:30:59.901
I will.

00:31:02.046 --> 00:31:03.299
She'll come after me.

00:31:05.242 --> 00:31:07.111
All right, you know what? That's it.

00:31:17.349 --> 00:31:18.730
This is about Jessica, isn't it?

00:31:22.935 --> 00:31:24.252
You think that's your
dirty little secret,

00:31:24.273 --> 00:31:26.100
That you killed her somehow?

00:31:29.345 --> 00:31:31.511
Sam, this has got to stop, man.

00:31:33.146 --> 00:31:33.953
I mean,

00:31:34.315 --> 00:31:35.674
The nightmares and-And

00:31:35.790 --> 00:31:37.808
Calling her name out in
the middle of the night,

00:31:38.615 --> 00:31:39.974
It's gonna kill you.

00:31:41.291 --> 00:31:42.353
Now, listen to me.

00:31:43.755 --> 00:31:45.241
It wasn't your fault.

00:31:46.715 --> 00:31:49.519
If you want to blame something,
then blame the thing that killed her.

00:31:49.986 --> 00:31:51.473
Or, hell, why don't
you take a swing at me?

00:31:51.515 --> 00:31:54.000
I'm the one that dragged you
away from her the first place.

00:31:54.213 --> 00:31:55.360
I don't blame you.

00:31:55.905 --> 00:31:57.200
You shouldn't blame yourself,

00:31:57.625 --> 00:31:59.260
Because there's
nothingyou could've done.

00:31:59.409 --> 00:32:01.108
I could've warned her. About what?!

00:32:01.899 --> 00:32:03.556
You didn't know what was gonna happen.

00:32:05.000 --> 00:32:06.104
And, besides,

00:32:06.274 --> 00:32:08.366
All of this isn't a secret.
I mean, I know all about it.

00:32:08.377 --> 00:32:09.906
It's not gonna work with Mary anyway.

00:32:10.235 --> 00:32:11.234
No, you don't.

00:32:12.720 --> 00:32:13.294
I don't what?

00:32:13.379 --> 00:32:15.630
You don't know all about it.

00:32:16.352 --> 00:32:17.775
I haven't told you everything.

00:32:19.943 --> 00:32:21.005
What are you talking about?

00:32:21.833 --> 00:32:23.978
It wouldn't really be a
secret if I told you, would it?

00:32:31.207 --> 00:32:31.950
No.

00:32:33.373 --> 00:32:34.414
I don't like it.

00:32:34.435 --> 00:32:35.986
It's not gonna happen. Forget it.

00:32:36.708 --> 00:32:38.917
Dean, that girl back
there is going to die

00:32:39.972 --> 00:32:41.777
Unless we do something about it.

00:32:42.563 --> 00:32:43.349
And you know what?

00:32:43.731 --> 00:32:46.641
Who knows how many more people
are gonna die after that?

00:32:48.107 --> 00:32:49.190
Now, we're doing this.

00:32:52.025 --> 00:32:54.213
You've got to let me do this.

00:33:21.813 --> 00:33:24.043
Well, that's just great.

00:33:33.834 --> 00:33:35.427
All right, let's start looking.

00:34:14.250 --> 00:34:15.822
Maybe they've already sold it.

00:34:21.525 --> 00:34:22.672
I don't think so.

00:34:35.304 --> 00:34:36.303
That's it.

00:34:39.361 --> 00:34:40.572
You sure about this?

00:34:57.467 --> 00:34:58.444
Bloody Mary.

00:35:01.545 --> 00:35:02.607
Bloody Mary.

00:35:14.223 --> 00:35:15.052
Bloody Mary.

00:35:25.360 --> 00:35:27.251
I'll go check that out.
Stay here. Be careful.

00:35:29.618 --> 00:35:31.254
Smash anything that moves.

00:35:42.610 --> 00:35:43.502
Crap.

00:36:02.036 --> 00:36:02.991
Hold on

00:36:03.246 --> 00:36:05.816
Whoa, guys, false alarm.

00:36:06.326 --> 00:36:07.473
I tripped the system.

00:36:07.590 --> 00:36:08.482
Who are you?

00:36:09.161 --> 00:36:10.266
I'm the boss's kid.

00:36:12.007 --> 00:36:13.452
You're Mr. Yamashiro's kid?

00:36:29.116 --> 00:36:30.199
Come on.

00:36:31.324 --> 00:36:32.535
Come into this one.

00:36:56.270 --> 00:36:57.321
It's your fault.

00:36:58.766 --> 00:36:59.849
You killed her.

00:37:03.566 --> 00:37:04.861
You killed Jessica.

00:37:08.492 --> 00:37:10.297
Like I said, I was adopted.

00:37:11.072 --> 00:37:11.858
Yeah.

00:37:14.577 --> 00:37:15.596
You know, I just

00:37:16.287 --> 00:37:18.432
I really don't have
timefor this right now.

00:37:24.485 --> 00:37:25.823
You never told her the truth,

00:37:26.513 --> 00:37:27.724
Who you really were.

00:37:28.467 --> 00:37:30.166
But it's more than that,isn't it?

00:37:31.122 --> 00:37:32.715
Those nightmares you've been having

00:37:33.150 --> 00:37:34.658
Of jessica dying,

00:37:35.104 --> 00:37:36.060
Screaming,

00:37:36.952 --> 00:37:37.823
Burning

00:37:38.524 --> 00:37:40.796
You had them for days before she died.

00:37:41.784 --> 00:37:42.804
Didn't you?!

00:37:45.352 --> 00:37:47.264
You were so desperateto ignore them,

00:37:47.285 --> 00:37:49.006
To believethey were just dreams.

00:37:49.664 --> 00:37:51.140
How could you ignore them like that?

00:37:51.777 --> 00:37:54.283
How could you leave her alone to die?

00:37:57.129 --> 00:37:58.786
You dreamt it would happen!

00:38:05.478 --> 00:38:06.264
Dude.

00:38:06.837 --> 00:38:08.281
Sammy, sammy!

00:38:10.161 --> 00:38:11.053
It's sam.

00:38:12.845 --> 00:38:14.035
God, are you okay?

00:38:14.226 --> 00:38:15.118
Uh, yeah.

00:38:17.157 --> 00:38:18.049
Come on, come on.

00:39:21.127 --> 00:39:23.272
You killed them!

00:39:23.718 --> 00:39:25.418
All those people!

00:39:25.803 --> 00:39:27.991
You killed them!

00:39:56.510 --> 00:39:57.402
Hey, sam?

00:39:58.332 --> 00:39:59.118
Yeah?

00:40:00.530 --> 00:40:03.674
That's got to be like
what, 600 years of bad luck?

00:40:28.039 --> 00:40:29.377
So this is really over?

00:40:31.227 --> 00:40:32.268
Yeah, it's over.

00:40:34.498 --> 00:40:35.348
Thank you.

00:40:47.261 --> 00:40:48.110
Charlie?

00:40:52.144 --> 00:40:53.546
Your boyfriend's death,

00:40:54.799 --> 00:40:56.561
You really should try
to forgive yourself.

00:40:57.326 --> 00:40:58.367
No matter what you did,

00:40:58.834 --> 00:41:00.066
You probably couldn't have stopped it.

00:41:02.561 --> 00:41:04.091
Sometimes bad things just happen.

00:41:15.775 --> 00:41:16.742
That's good advice.

00:41:33.272 --> 00:41:34.101
Hey, sam?

00:41:35.163 --> 00:41:35.800
Yeah?

00:41:36.788 --> 00:41:38.359
Now that this is all over,

00:41:39.336 --> 00:41:41.078
I want you to tell me
what that secret is.

00:41:46.016 --> 00:41:46.950
Look...

00:41:48.469 --> 00:41:49.467
You're my brother.

00:41:50.848 --> 00:41:52.165
And I'd die for you.

00:41:54.830 --> 00:41:56.869
But there are some things
I need to keep to myself.



00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:22.000
